{"title":"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Punxsutawney_Phil\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Punxsutawney Phil</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For every real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/1/441416e660d25335f27e55334ac2a06e51541c97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"19\" /> denote the greatest integer not exceeding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/d/b6d01f35e21f4dda60a2836b577dcbd218144d36.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x)=\\lfloor x\\rfloor(2014^{x-\\lfloor x\\rfloor}-1).\\]\" width=\"209\" height=\"21\" />  The set of all numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/a/e9a30e64bd0df3bbbbd252212e1ee9dd63a91bfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\leq x&lt;2014$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"104\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/d/0bd18b45fb03ac6400611a4ecb03d4f1c68b79ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)\\leq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> is a union of disjoint intervals.  What is the sum of the lengths of those intervals?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/5/355d7836eeeb58e14d0ba99e0ea8bb7662a69b6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }1\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }\\dfrac{\\log 2015}{\\log 2014}\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }\\dfrac{\\log 2014}{\\log 2013}\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }\\dfrac{2014}{2013}\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }2014^{\\frac1{2014}}\\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"552\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/0/2f08d31025b828f4d974161059823f37a1430642.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x\\rfloor=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"19\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/1/901ea17d6554373d93231f63ed1a235c84bb3f3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\leq k\\leq 2013$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />.  Then we can rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/8/60865d45e6005041ec3eeba5c2880e7e37793183.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k(2014^{x-k}-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"116\" height=\"20\" />.  In order for this to be less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/5/9c552ebb523b7c4902dcb1292d22b7f94a658d1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2014^{x-k}-1\\leq\\dfrac1k\\implies x\\leq k+\\log_{2014}\\left(\\dfrac{k+1}k\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"370\" height=\"43\" />.  Combining this with the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/4/eb4b45aa9acc9f13a7d1d6fbfbbe9e3e3eabfaf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x\\rfloor =k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"19\" /> gives that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/6/f166eefdf28e0d71694031656161e036fb398b86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in\\left[k,k+\\log_{2014}\\left(\\dfrac{k+1}k\\right)\\right]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"222\" height=\"43\" />, and so the length of the interval is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/2/d52a7e22d0a1cc4f25809029b29a4795930504fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{2014}\\left(\\dfrac{k+1}k\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"121\" height=\"43\" />.  We want the sum of all possible intervals such that the inequality holds true; since all of these intervals must be disjoint, we can sum from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed8470bc717a49aafe4556c7e2c2e11ddc7b687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/5/ba59dfa9ae5ff4c01ce2ed06e8cba5eda691c684.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=2013$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" /> to get that the desired sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/2/06261d18b68a17761cb48e3ae0a8834f53752c6b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^{2013}\\log_{2014}\\left(\\dfrac{i+1}i\\right)=\\log_{2014}\\left(\\prod_{i=1}^{2013}\\dfrac{i+1}i\\right)=\\log_{2014}\\left(\\dfrac{2014}1\\right)=\\boxed{1\\textbf{ (A)}}.\\]\" width=\"556\" height=\"53\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/videos/amc/2014amc12a/380\">https://artofproblemsolving.com/videos/amc/2014amc12a/380</a>\n</p><p>~ dolphin7\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Punxsutawney_Phil\">Video Solution by Punxsutawney Phil</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Punxsutawney Phil\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtube.com/watch?v=MI3ax4WJBZA\">https://youtube.com/watch?v=MI3ax4WJBZA</a>\n</p><p>(The video is no longer available on YouTube)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A\">2014 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_1